This discussion focused on developing a methods section for incorporating "Variability and extreme events" into a report on flooding impacts. The user outlined the need to combine historical flood damage data from UK reports and EM-DAT with climate-driven damage projections. Key tasks included constructing an empirical set of monthly damages, fitting statistical distributions (log-normal, exponential, Weibull, Generalized Extreme Value) to these damages, and modeling the annual frequency of events using a Poisson process. The outcomes aimed to estimate expected annual damages (EAD) and 1-in-200 year extreme event damages to enhance the understanding of flood risk under climate scenarios, while avoiding detailed explanations of these definitions, as they would be covered in another section.
